<binaryimage arch="V850:LE:32:default">
<!--
    GH-8817: V850 "jmp [reg]" switch dispatch not recovered as a jumptable.
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/8817
    (GayHydra #477; kuna tests/stages/gh8817-v850indbranch.xml)

    Upstream's V850 SLEIGH lifted "jmp [reg]" (reg != lp) to "call [reg]"
    (CPUI_CALLIND).  Jump-table recovery only runs on CPUI_BRANCHIND, so a
    bounded compiler switch dispatch
        cmp 2,r10 ; bh default
        mov table,r11 ; shl 2,r10 ; add r11,r10 ; ld.w 0[r10],r10
        add r11,r10 ; jmp [r10]
    rendered as a computed call through a function pointer.  kuna fixes this
    in the decompiler with the default-off option v850indirectbranch, which
    reclassifies that CALLIND to BRANCHIND at flow time.

    The fork does not need the option: its V850 spec already lifts
    "jmp [reg]" to "goto [R0004]" (Instructions/Special.sinc, since the port
    of upstream PR 8996 in GayHydra PR 146), so the dispatch is a BRANCHIND
    and the stock pipeline recovers the switch.  kuna's option line is
    therefore dropped and the assertions pin the recovered switch and the
    absence of the computed call.  The test can only run once the cspec
    spells the CTBP register correctly (GayHydra #509).

    The 3-entry jump table lives at 0x2200 (4-byte LE entries, each an offset
    added to the 0x2200 table base):
        0x2200: 0xFFFFFF1E, case 0 stub at 0x211e (mov 1,r10 ; jmp [lp])
        0x2204: 0xFFFFFF22, case 1 stub at 0x2122 (mov 2,r10 ; jmp [lp])
        0x2208: 0xFFFFFF26, case 2 stub at 0x2126 (mov 3,r10 ; jmp [lp])
    with the default stub at 0x211a (mov 9,r10 ; jmp [lp]).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x2104">
